node_modules/
package-lock.json

# NOTE: `dist/` is deliberately NOT ignored — its four build outputs
# (aleph_panel.js, aleph_panel_bg.wasm, index.html, tailwind.css) are TRACKED,
# and that is load-bearing:
#
#   * .github/workflows/aleph-app-release.yml embeds them verbatim — read the
#     comment above the desktop-app matrix: "Panel WASM dist is pre-built and
#     committed to git — no WASM build here." No release job owns a WASM
#     toolchain, so an empty dist/ ships an empty Panel.
#   * scripts/check_panel_dist.mjs (CI `Panel dist pairing`, and `needs:` of
#     every release build) verifies the committed js+wasm are a matched pair.
#
# They look exactly like the generated artifacts they are, so "these were never
# source, never reviewed" is a true and insufficient reason to drop them: that
# happened at 033814185 (2026-08-13) and left the release pipeline gated shut
# for two days. If you want dist/ untracked, the same change must teach the
# release workflow to build the WASM first — then delete this block.
#
# Regenerate with `just wasm` (never a js-only rebuild — see check_panel_dist).
